  "title": "Avoiding endless scroll",
  "description": "Have you ever tried to pick your country from a drop-down on a mobile phone? It&#8217;s either endless &#8220;wheeling&#8221; or scrolling. It&#8217;s painful. Especially if you live in Zimbabwe! And ",
  "slug": "avoiding-endless-scroll",
  "url": "https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/2015/11/18/avoiding-endless-scroll/",
  "path": "/avoiding-endless-scroll",
  "canonical_url": "https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/2015/11/18/avoiding-endless-scroll/",
  "body_html": "<p>Have you ever tried to pick your country from a drop-down on a mobile phone?<br />\nIt&#8217;s either endless &#8220;wheeling&#8221; or scrolling. It&#8217;s painful.<br />\nEspecially if you live in Zimbabwe!<br />\nAnd when you finally reach your country, you&#8217;re too exhausted to click it.</p>\n<p>HTML5 introduced a new element, the &lt;datalist&gt;, which, unfortunately, is not used that many places — yet!</p>\n<p>It&#8217;s basically a list:</p>\n<pre class=\"brush: xml; title: ; notranslate\" title=\"\">\r\n&lt;datalist id=&quot;country-select-datalist&quot;&gt;\r\n  &lt;option&gt;Armenia&lt;/option&gt;\r\n  &lt;option&gt;Bahrain&lt;/option&gt;\r\n  ...\r\n&lt;/datalist&gt;\r\n</pre>\n<p>That&#8217;s associated with an &lt;input&gt;-field:</p>\n<pre class=\"brush: xml; title: ; notranslate\" title=\"\">\r\n&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; list=&quot;country-select-datalist&quot;&gt;\r\n</pre>\n<p>The result is this:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/datalist.png\"><img loading=\"lazy\" data-attachment-id=\"467\" data-permalink=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/2015/11/18/avoiding-endless-scroll/datalist/\" data-orig-file=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/datalist.png\" data-orig-size=\"297,147\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"datalist\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-medium-file=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/datalist.png?w=297\" data-large-file=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/datalist.png?w=297\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-467\" src=\"assets/wp-460/b0bcff01.png\" alt=\"datalist\" width=\"297\" height=\"147\" srcset=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/datalist.png 297w, https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/datalist.png?w=150&amp;h=74 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 297px) 100vw, 297px\" /></a></p>\n<p>All browsers — except Safari — supports &lt;datalist&gt;. Even Internet Explorer 10!<br />\nIt&#8217;s a nice, fast and JavaScript-free autosuggest.</p>\n<p>For Safari, there are plenty of polyfills to make datalist work, among them Lea Verous <a href=\"http://leaverou.github.io/awesomplete/\" target=\"_blank\">Awesomplete</a>, which is very easy to work with.</p>\n<p>If you&#8217;re using the structure above (there are other options as well), all you have to do, is add the class &#8220;awesomplete&#8221; to the &lt;input&gt;-field:</p>\n<pre class=\"brush: xml; title: ; notranslate\" title=\"\">\r\n&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; list=&quot;country-select-datalist&quot; class=&quot;awesomplete&quot;&gt;\r\n</pre>\n<p>The result is slightly different:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/awesomplete.png\"><img loading=\"lazy\" data-attachment-id=\"466\" data-permalink=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/2015/11/18/avoiding-endless-scroll/awesomplete/\" data-orig-file=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/awesomplete.png\" data-orig-size=\"303,125\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"awesomplete\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-medium-file=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/awesomplete.png?w=300\" data-large-file=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/awesomplete.png?w=303\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-466\" src=\"assets/wp-460/62d478c4.png\" alt=\"awesomplete\" width=\"303\" height=\"125\" srcset=\"https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/awesomplete.png 303w, https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/awesomplete.png?w=150&amp;h=62 150w, https://madsstoumann.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/awesomplete.png?w=300&amp;h=124 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 303px) 100vw, 303px\" /></a></p>\n<p>For structured markup, you can add the <em>ListItem</em>-schema:</p>\n<pre class=\"brush: xml; title: ; notranslate\" title=\"\">\r\n&lt;datalist id=&quot;country-select-datalist&quot; itemscope=&quot;&quot; itemtype=&quot;http://schema.org/ListItem&quot;&gt;\r\n  &lt;option itemprop=&quot;name&quot;&gt;Armenia&lt;/option&gt;\r\n  &lt;option itemprop=&quot;name&quot;&gt;Bahrain&lt;/option&gt;\r\n ...\r\n&lt;/datalist&gt;\r\n</pre>\n<p>Happy coding!</p>\n",
